---
description: Tests assert behaviour given conditions, not styling or file presence
globs: ["**/*.{test,spec}.{ts,tsx}"]
alwaysApply: false
---

Tests assert behaviour given conditions, not styling and not the
presence or absence of files or components.

Examples of the right shape:

- Given a list payload that omits the total, the UI does not present
  $0.00 as a verified sum; a loaded empty set may still show $0.00.
- Given a submit or discard is in flight, a second click does not start
  another mutation (or the action is not operable).
- After a successful save, the list (or other visible state) reflects
  the new data once the mutation settles.
- Given a dialog or sheet is open, it has an accessible name.

Do not assert classNames, computed styles, or screenshots. Do not write
a test whose only job is to check that a helper, file, or component
still exists. A test that only checks a mock was called, or that the
component rendered, is not a regression test.

eslint-plugin-testing-library (prefer-user-event, awaited finds, no
container/node access) is how we drive and query the UI. It does not
replace the cases above and cannot require a second-click case on its
own.

See `apps/web/src/test/README.md` and `expectOpenOverlayNamed` in
`apps/web/src/test/behaviour.ts`.
